Hi,

A late summary because it took me a long time to find out how to resolv 
the problem, and i still do not have all the answers...

Why Tru64 needs a reboot to recognise the Hitachi is still a mistery.


If i use Lun 0 and 2 different host groups all the luns attached to that 
machine gets 'blocked'. To resolv this I need to run the following 
commands on each cluster member and then release that lun from that 
member:
scu> sbtl 5 5 0
Device: HSG80, Bus: 5, Target: 5, Lun: 0, Type: Direct Access
scu>  reset device
scu> pres register key 0 skey 1
scu> pres clear key 1

I am still waiting on the official answer from Sun (where we bought the 
Hitachi) about Lun0 and how to use the host groups in a cluster.
But not using lun0 and placing all the members in the same host group is 
working ok at the moment.

Peter Jakobs




