The answer came from Xerox.

Add the following service in /etc/services:

repro 9100/tcp

With that printer configuration in /etc/printcap: the key is the lp and rp =
parameters.  lp define the service to use in the services files and  rp =
the name of the print queue.

REPRO2|xerox2|lp11|repro2:\
        :lf=3D/usr/adm/lp11err:\
        :lp=3D@xerox-repro2/repro:\
        :mx#0:\
        :of=3D/usr/lbin/lpf:\
        :pl#66:\
        :pw#80:\
        :rm=3DXerox-Repro2:\
        :rp=3Dprint:\
        :sd=3D/usr/spool/lpd11:\
        :xf=3D/usr/lbin/xf:



