Has anyone had issues with SNMP being unreliable when
the Oracle agent takes over for Tru64?  I had an ES40
w 5.1A PK6 that was answering to SNMP gets every
minute for basic system and netowrk OIDs that were
part of the default DEC MIB.  Once the Oracle wrapper
was put around it (per Oracle specs), both the system
and Oracle OIDs became unreliable.  The behavior is
that every so often a request will fail for that
interval, but the very next interval it will succeed
(most are at 1 minute intervals).  At any given time,
I would estimate that only 60-70% all the Oracle and
DEC are valid.

If somebody who has gotten Oracle SNMP to work on
Tru64, I would be happy to provide all the information
on our configuration, but that's a lot of data for
this email.

